GMEM off unless asked for. The plug-in tiled every pass of 56 draws or more by default (`metal_gmem_draws` 56 when not
given, and `hakios_metal_cb_set_gmem(cb, hm_gmem_on() || hm_gmem_draws() != 0)`), with the hardware's binning: that path
leaves tiles with the frame before (gpu-p2, 2026-11-12: the home screen's labels twice, icons cut at the tile seams;
gpu-v6: the Control Center's glass flat, its glyphs garbled) and costs the GPU 11-13 ms for SpringBoard's 70-85-draw
passes against 4.9-5.4 in sysmem (gpu-p4 against gpu-p1, same root). Without binning the picture is right but every
draw runs in every one of the 76 tiles and CoreAnimation falls to one frame a second (gpu-p1, gpu-p3). So: no GMEM by
default; `metal_gmem=1` or `metal_gmem_draws=N` turn it back on as before, for the day the binning is right.

